# Cloudflare redirects.
#
# This file is deliberately comments-only, and that is not an oversight.
#
# What used to be here, and why both lines had to go:
#
#   /api/*  https://<backend>/api/:splat  200     <- REJECTED
#   /*      /index.html                   200     <- REJECTED
#
# 1. Cloudflare cannot proxy to an external host. A 200 rewrite may only point
#    at a relative path, so the deploy fails with:
#      "Proxy (200) redirects can only point to relative paths.
#       Got https://<backend>/api/:splat"
#    The docs are explicit: "Proxying will only support relative URLs on your
#    site. You cannot proxy external domains." Only a Cloudflare Worker script
#    can proxy off-platform, and this project has no Worker script.
#
#    So the browser calls the backend directly and the backend allows this
#    origin through CORS. See docs/DEPLOY.md.
#
# 2. `/* /index.html 200` is rejected as an infinite loop:
#      "Infinite loop detected in this rule. This would cause a redirect to
#       strip `.html` or `/index` and end up triggering this rule again."
#    SPA routing is configured in wrangler.jsonc instead, via
#    assets.not_found_handling = "single-page-application". That is the
#    supported mechanism on Workers; without it, deep links like /figur/1 404.
#
# If you deploy to Netlify instead, add this one line back:
#
#   /*  /index.html  200
#
# Do NOT add the /api/* proxy line back on Cloudflare. It cannot work.
